{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1788032076643262001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"peaceable-choppy-sapsucker","assignee":null,"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":3,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"e1a891e8a8e4c74b5a2013e5967aa039bf1c521933564402f62d0f4a4b6c26c8","event_uuid":"d1fd303b-3853-4c31-82c8-f883f047e9f7","position":{"commit_sha":"ce0571b71e60d5095db4c16484d7bb3c284e854b","position":"1788029163626078078-d1fd303b-3853-4c31-82c8-f883f047e9f7"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"9993563f01e92fb45ca7bdb0820c0005e67b7efdea3c00aefb3700978f986036","event_uuid":"539dab70-2a6e-43eb-993f-26bf7db2281d","position":{"commit_sha":"cbe673c0cdeb44b85f60fc72c8c26286e468739b","position":"1788029282039411496-539dab70-2a6e-43eb-993f-26bf7db2281d"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"c46cf5af05727a1490dabc308fe6d5171136ee638c28e612d4bd68ea3a781b6a","event_uuid":"aaf4ba11-67b9-416c-8b0b-aa50d0c49119","position":{"commit_sha":"1a04188c3b29c20df44cfeba326fccb083f7335c","position":"1788029598603963380-aaf4ba11-67b9-416c-8b0b-aa50d0c49119"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1788029163626078078,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"539dab70-2a6e-43eb-993f-26bf7db2281d","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"53ab-bdf6-de1c-4bb1"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nPass 1 (`src/rebar/llm/plan_review/pass1.py`, `passes.pass1_chunk`, prompts `reviewers/plan_review_finder.md` + one `plan_review_<ID>.md` per criterion, routing in `criteria_routing.json` + `.rebar/criteria_routing.json`, frontier class = Opus on Bedrock) is the expensive pass (~$3.4/review uncached, ~12 finder calls). A criterion edit cannot be judged from stored data alone, so Tier 2 re-runs finders on a small fixed sample and then runs Tier 1 on the new findings so the whole chain is measured. Per-criterion edits are far cheaper in single-criterion mode (one single-turn call ≈ $0.17 at 30k Opus input), and prior work (`docs/experiments/plan-review-model-tradeoff.md`) showed Opus is flat to 12 criteria/turn while Sonnet degrades — which is why the production model must be used.\n\n## Approach\n\nBuild `src/rebar/llm/evals/plan_replay/tier2.py`:\n\n- **Fixed sample**: a committed list of ~20 review ids drawn once by the Tier-1 stratified sampler (with the additional stratum: at least 5 containers, at least 8 with ≥10 findings, at least 3 from the LMN store), stored as `docs/experiments/plan-review-gate/replay/tier2-sample.json` so every proposal is measured on the same plans. Plan text comes from the reconstructed material; code-grounded AGENT criteria run against the pinned `verified_at_sha` snapshot via the existing `source=attested` mechanics.\n- **Full mode**: run the candidate registry/prompts through `ProductionBatchRunner`/`run_pass1` with the frontier class pinned to Bedrock Opus; compare finding sets to the stored Pass-1 findings by `norm_id` (Jaccard, gained/lost per criterion), then run Tier 1 (current questions) on the candidate findings and Tier 0 downstream.\n- **Single-criterion mode**: `--criteria T5c` runs only the named criteria (single-turn chunk of one, via the same seam `probe_criteria` uses) on the sample and compares only that criterion's findings; cost ≈ N × $0.17.\n- The baseline for a criterion whose stored findings were produced under a different `regver` is a one-time baseline run recorded in the ledger; otherwise the stored findings are the baseline.\n- Budget pre-flight from stored per-criterion usage (`coverage.usage.per_criterion`) × current price.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/llm/evals/plan_replay/tier2.py` (new)\n- `docs/experiments/plan-review-gate/replay/tier2-sample.json`, `tier2-*.md` (new/generated)\n- `tests/unit/evals/test_plan_replay_tier2.py` (new)\n\n## Testing\n\nUnit: with a `FakeRunner` returning canned `P1Output`, gained/lost findings per criterion match expectations; single-criterion mode issues exactly one chunk per sampled review containing only the requested criterion; a run is refused when the frontier model is not the Bedrock Opus id; the sample file is validated against the corpus manifest. Live (commissioning, ≤$60): one full-mode baseline over the fixed sample.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] A committed fixed sample of review ids exists with the strata above; checked by the sample file and manifest cross-check.\n- [ ] `tier2 --candidate <registry-dir>` produces finding-set Jaccard and gained/lost-per-criterion tables plus downstream Tier-1/Tier-0 metrics; checked by one generated report.\n- [ ] `tier2 --criteria <id>` costs ≤ N × $0.25 in the ledger for a single-turn criterion; checked by the ledger.\n- [ ] Commissioning spend for this ticket ≤ $60 and every call uses the Bedrock frontier model id; checked by the ledger.\n- [ ] Unit tests pass in `make test`.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/llm/evals/plan_replay/tier2.py","reason":"Pass-1 replay + single-criterion mode"},{"path":"docs/experiments/plan-review-gate/replay/tier2-sample.json","reason":"fixed sample"},{"path":"docs/experiments/plan-review-gate/replay/","reason":"generated reports"},{"path":"tests/unit/evals/test_plan_replay_tier2.py","reason":"unit tests"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["depends_on","53ab-bdf6-de1c-4bb1"],["parent","759e-7dc1-675c-4877"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"759e-7dc1-675c-4877","parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["plan-review","evals","tier-2","pass-1"],"ticket_id":"f1d6-cfcc-a9c6-416d","ticket_type":"story","title":"Tier-2 harness: replay Pass-1 criteria on a fixed stratified sample (Opus via Bedrock, budgeted; single-criterion mode)","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["d1fd303b-3853-4c31-82c8-f883f047e9f7","539dab70-2a6e-43eb-993f-26bf7db2281d","aaf4ba11-67b9-416c-8b0b-aa50d0c49119"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788032076643262001,"uuid":"7b541c93-082b-4573-86f2-c2f7dfb64e4d"}